# Build output — everything here is reproducible from source.
# Note: patterns are matched case-insensitively on macOS (core.ignoreCase), so
# bare artifact names like "Image" or "vmlinux" must never appear unanchored —
# "Image" would swallow the whole image/ tree.
/bin/
/out/

# Buildroot working trees, if BUILD_DIR is pointed back into the repo. The
# default keeps them on local disk outside the repo (see Makefile).
/image/buildroot-*/
/image/.stamp-*

# Built artifacts
*.ext4
*.img

# Go
*.test
*.out
# `go build ./tools/...` drops its binary in the working directory.
/gendocs
# Same for tools/sbom — release-sbom invokes it with `go run`, so a built
# binary here is a stray artifact, not something the build needs committed.
/sbom

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Release staging — regenerated by `make release-artifacts`.
/dist/

# Proof output. dev/demo-team.sh writes its exported transcript where the
# person who ran it will find it, which in CI is what the workflow uploads.
/team.html
/*.log

# Local tool settings, not project configuration. The skills directory is the
# exception: a skill is a committed procedure, like the scripts under dev/.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/

# The seccomp probe leaves what it observed here when no record for this
# architecture is committed yet; the record itself is tracked.
/dev/expect/*.observed

# Process documents, kept beside the repository rather than in it. The working
# tracker, its closed predecessor and the one-page status are how the work is
# run; what the work decided lives in docs/decisions.md, what it built in
# docs/roadmap.md, and what changed in CHANGELOG.md — all of which are here and
# all of which the source cites. A reader of this project needs those; nobody
# needs a progress log of who ran which command on which afternoon.
/PLAN.html
/PLAN-FEATURES.html
/STATUS.md
/tools/check-plan.py

# Working documents that are not project documentation: security reviews and
# audits, testing plans, handoff briefs, agent prompts, scratch notes. They are
# point-in-time artefacts for whoever is acting on them, and what actually
# changed and why belongs in CHANGELOG.md and docs/decisions.md, in the commit
# that changed it — not in a report that will be stale next week.
#
# One directory rather than a rule per filename, because the rules below were
# written one incident at a time and a document whose name nobody predicted is
# a document that gets committed by a stray `git add -A`. Put it in local/ and
# the question does not arise.
#
# Not for: PLAN.html, PLAN-FEATURES.html, STATUS.md and team.html, which stay
# at the root because committed things point at them there — CLAUDE.md and
# README.md name PLAN.html, tools/check-plan.py resolves it as a sibling of
# tools/ (check-plan.py:15), and caps.yml and dev/demo-team.sh reach for the
# others. Moving them would break a reference to buy tidiness.
/local/

# The filename rules that predate local/. Kept rather than replaced: they cost
# nothing, and they still catch a review dropped in the root out of habit.
/SECURITY-REVIEW.html
/SECURITY-REVIEW-*.html
/SECURITY-AUDIT-*.html
/SECURITY-TESTING-PLAN*.html
/SECURITY_AUDIT.md
/PEN_TEST_REPORT.md
/dev/docs-audit-*.md
